==Throws==
====Forward Throw====
{{FrameDataCargo-COTW
|name=Ko Satsu Shou
|moveId=nightmaregeese_throw
|description=Geese grabs the opponent by the neck and launches them off with a palm strike.
* When used midscreen, throws the opponent 3/4 of the screen away. You can meaty their wakeup with a 236C.
* In the corner, any safe jump has to be manually timed, but a Reppuu Ken feint allows you to time a meaty, reversal-safe 236A on their wakeup, locking them down for more pressure. 
Despite how far away this appears to throw them, you have a generous window to push okizeme after the throw. Not only can you easily meaty the opponent with a fireball, but two dashes sets the opponent up perfectly for a mixup using far D whiff cancel. 
In the corner, while the knockdown time is the same as Explosion Ball, the okizeme is even better due to the distance Geese is left afterward. You basically get to do whatever you want as a mixup there.
}}

====Back Throw====
{{FrameDataCargo-COTW
|name=Shinkuu Nage
|moveId=nightmaregeese_4throw
|description=Geese tosses the opponent over his shoulder, similarly to his command grab from the older games. 
* When used midscreen, throws the opponent almost an entire screen's length away. You can meaty the opponent's wakeup with a 236A. 
* In the corner, any safe jump has to be manually timed, but two dashes or an empty fullhop gives you a meaty close heavy, 2C or 5AC.
Geese's back throw switches sides, though the okizeme isn’t quite as good as his forward throw. You can safely meaty the opponent's wakeup with a Reppuken, which effortlessly sets up your zoning or potentially forces the opponent into a checkmate. 
