====Hishou Nichirin Zan====
{{FrameDataCargo-COTW
|moveId=nightmaregeese_623A,nightmaregeese_623C,nightmaregeese_623AC
|input=623A/C/AC
|input2=dp+A/C/AC
|description3=Nightmare Geese leaps up into the air and slashes downward. 
Despite its DP input and its similarity to DP type special moves, this move is NOT invincible nor a good anti-air; rather, Hishou Nichirin Zan is another tool in Nightmare Geese's bag of mixup tricks.

* All versions can be Braked on startup, which will make Nightmare Geese leap into the air without performing the slash. This can be useful for empty jump low mixups, especially when done after knockdowns and setups.

----
'''Light Version''' (623A)

* Numbers in [square brakets] denote values when it hits an opponent in the air.

* The Light version is a safe blockstring ender, though there is a decently-sized gap between any normal cancelled into this move and when the move hits. It cannot hit crossup.

* The frame advantage for this move varies depending on if the opponent blocked it standing or crouching; on standing block it's -2, on crouching block it's 0. Additionally, if spaced properly (about two backdashes away from the opponent) it can become +2 on both standing and crouching block.

* The Light version can hit airborne opponents on the way up and knock them down with the slash hit. The first hit does not connect on grounded opponents and can make for an okay anti-air, though since it has no invincibility of any kind it can be stuffed or trade with the opponent's air buttons. It can be used as a combo ender in situations where Fudou Ken will not work due to having been used earlier in the combo.

* As the startup of all versions of this move can be Braked, this means that Nightmare Geese can get a psuedo-DP Brake combo if he connects with the airborne-only first hit and Brakes. At most heights he won't be able to actually juggle into anything outside of his Hidden Gear, but at higher juggle heights (like those granted by a Counter Hit Heavy Fudou Ken for example) he has just enough time to juggle a Light Hishou Nichiran Zan Brake into Raging Storm, Deadly Rave, or even Light Fudou Ken at the highest juggle.


----
'''Heavy Version (623C)'''
* A swiss army knife of a special move that can act as an overhead, a pressure reset, a crossup, a meaty, and a hard projectile callout in just one move.

* At 35 frames of startup this move can unfortunately be reacted to very easily, whether by the opponent blocking correctly or by an anti-air. To compensate, Nightmare Geese travels about half the screen and it is always plus on block and able to continue his pressure, though how plus he is differs depending on spacing and if it hit meaty or not.

* =3 on block if done at close range/as a crossup, around +5-6 on block if spaced from two backwards hops away, and +9 on block if spaced to hit at the very tip.

* +5 on standing hit, allowing for a link into Far A. If Nightmare Geese does manage to hit a crouching (read: sleeping) opponent with this move, he'll be +9 (+8 on crossup) and be able to link into 2C. 

* On Counter Hit/Wild Punish Nightmare Geese will be +10 and can link into 2C. Nightmare Geese can put himself in this situation if he preemptively leaps over a projectile with this move and hits the opponent during their projectile recovery. With a healthy amount of REV to spend, at least one bar of super meter and S.P.G. state, Nightmare Geese can get immensely damaging combos out of one good read like this.

----
'''REV Version (623AC)'''

* Similar to the Heavy version in that it's an overhead and is plus on block. Starts up slightly faster but is still very reactable at 32 frames of startup. Has slightly more horizontal range as well.

* +2 on block if done at close range/as a crossup, +9 on block if spaced to hit at the very tip.

* +3 on standing hit, +7 on crouching hit. Nightmare Geese doesn't get much in the way of combos outside of Far B.

* REV Hishou Nichirin Zan is a good combo tool, as it ground bounces airborne opponents, usually after being REV Acceled from REV Reppuu Ken.
